WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.950
A chat assistant that
drafts a memo is a tool.

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:07.375
Nothing it does reaches a record until
a person reads the draft and acts.

3
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:08.813
An agent is different.

4
00:00:08.813 --> 00:00:13.762
It sends replies from a mailbox, closes
tickets and updates case records.

5
00:00:13.762 --> 00:00:16.297
Each step is an action
against agency data,

6
00:00:16.297 --> 00:00:19.700
taken by something that signed
in and holds permissions.

7
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.638
That makes an agent an identity.

8
00:00:21.638 --> 00:00:26.946
An AI system that acts reaches data
in one of four ways: on behalf of a

9
00:00:26.946 --> 00:00:32.062
signed-in user, as itself, as its own
user account, or with an A P I key.

10
00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:35.112
The first three run through
the identity provider.

11
00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:37.365
The fourth bypasses it entirely,

12
00:00:37.365 --> 00:00:41.787
so Conditional Access never applies
and no sign-in is evaluated.

13
00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:44.051
Today the agentic share is small.

14
00:00:44.051 --> 00:00:52.375
OMB's 2025 inventory holds 3,611
use cases, 445 of them high-impact.

15
00:00:52.375 --> 00:00:57.862
117 are classified agentic, and 38
of those are in pilot or deployed.

16
00:00:57.862 --> 00:01:00.340
It's also the share that grows fastest.
